# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore - Intelligent University Knowledge Assistant
#
# Rule of thumb applied here: ignore artefacts that a tool regenerates, and
# nothing that a human wrote. Every entry below is reproducible from source;
# nothing below is a decision, a requirement, or a measurement.
# ==============================================================================


# --- Virtual environments -----------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by `python -m venv .venv`. Never committed: it is ~7,400 files of
# third-party code, it is platform-specific, and it would dominate the repo.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Python bytecode ----------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated on every import. `.pyc` files also differ between Python versions
# and platforms, so committing them creates diff noise that hides real changes.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# --- Packaging and build output -----------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by `pip install -e .` / `python -m build`.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/

# --- Test and property-testing caches -----------------------------------------
# Local run state, not results. Test *outcomes* belong in the repository as
# documented claims; the cache that speeds up the next run does not.
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# --- Linter and type-checker caches -------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by `ruff` and `mypy`. Both are pure caches of analysis results.
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json

# --- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env` holds real credentials and must never enter history. Note that
# `.env.example` is deliberately NOT ignored: the template is documentation and
# is the reason a reviewer knows which variables the service reads.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key
!*.pub

# --- Agent / editor workspace state -------------------------------------------
# The AI coding workspace's own bookkeeping. Not part of the project.
.freebuff/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- Operating system cruft ---------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db

# --- Node (future React/TypeScript frontend, Phase 2+) ------------------------
# Listed now so the frontend cannot be added with an accidental 300 MB commit.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-store/

# --- Load-test and benchmark output -------------------------------------------
# Raw results are regenerated per run. Reproducibility comes from the harness,
# the pinned commit SHA and the recorded parameters - not from committing output.
.benchmarks/
reports/benchmark-*.json